## Third-party components and licensing notes

This project orchestrates external tools and services. Distribution of a packaged
build requires a fresh licensing review (PRD §19, open decision 2):

- **FFmpeg / ffprobe** — invoked as a separate process. FFmpeg is LGPL-2.1-or-later by
  default, but an LGPL build must be used and the licence text shipped; an
  `--enable-gpl` build (e.g. with libx264) is GPL-2.0-or-later and is what H.264
  encoding requires. Confirm the intended distribution model before bundling a binary.
- **x264** — GPL-2.0-or-later. Required for the H.264 output the MVP specifies.
- **Remotion** — named in the PRD as the intended composition engine for deterministic
  effects and titles. Remotion has its own commercial licensing terms that must be
  reviewed before distribution. The current export path uses FFmpeg filter graphs and
  does not depend on Remotion.
- **Tauri, React, Zustand, TanStack Query, zod** — MIT / Apache-2.0.

No provider API keys, model weights, or generated media are distributed with this
repository.
